.env
.venv/
.venv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
redteam_report.md
data/episodes.json
/tmp/

deploy/*.log
data/.asset_cache/

# Raw eval answers — regenerable, and large. REPORT.md is the artifact.
evals/results.jsonl
evals/search_results.jsonl

# Rendered clips are build output, not source.
clips/
data/.usage.json

# Lock and staging files from concurrent writes to data/episodes.json.
# Local coordination only — nothing another checkout needs.
*.lock
*.json.tmp

# Runtime state for the X bot: which mentions it has already answered.
# Machine-local, and committing it would make one deploy re-answer another's
# backlog.
data/x_bot_state.json
.broadcast-check.log
audio/
.models/
# Voice fingerprints -- 192-dimension embeddings of Ansem's and Banks's
# voices, sixteen per episode. Derived from audio anybody can download, so
# nothing here is secret, and regenerated in an evening by
# label_speakers.py. But a labelled voice template for a named person is
# not the same kind of thing as a transcript, and publishing one nobody
# asked us to publish is a decision rather than an oversight. It is also
# 42MB that the service never reads.
#
# data/speaker_map.json stays tracked: segment number to name, no vectors,
# and it is the part that took a human ear to produce.
data/speakers/
.claude/
data/sweeps/
.pytest_cache/
audio
